{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4WedderburnCoord","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4WedderburnCoord","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4Characters","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4BlockMap22","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4BlockMap31","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4BlockMap211","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":56,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.homVec_eq_mulVec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.homVec_eq_mulVec","kind":"theorem","line":1418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4WedderburnCoord.lean#L1418-L1544","doc":"**The stacked coordinates of the assembled map are the matrix action of\n`coordM` (sorry-free)** — 24 coordinate goals, each closed by `ring`\nafter unfolding: both sides are the same $A$-row applied to `v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.wedderburnInvV₄_eq_mulVec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.wedderburnInvV₄_eq_mulVec","kind":"theorem","line":1410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4WedderburnCoord.lean#L1410-L1415","doc":"Definitional glue (`rfl`): the inverse formulas are the `coordMInv`\naction on the stacked component vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.wedderburnInvV₄","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.wedderburnInvV₄","kind":"def","line":1403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4WedderburnCoord.lean#L1403-L1408","doc":"The inverse coordinate map, **defined** as the matrix action of the\nsymbolic inverse on the stacked component vector; the left/right\ninverse identities are proved in `HeckeH4WedderburnInv.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.homVec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.homVec","kind":"def","line":1397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4WedderburnCoord.lean#L1397-L1401","doc":"The stacked coordinates of the assembled Wedderburn map\n$(\\chi_+, \\chi_-, \\rho_{22}, \\rho_{31}, \\rho_{211})$ applied to `v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.wvec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.wvec","kind":"def","line":1391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4WedderburnCoord.lean#L1391-L1395","doc":"The stacked component vector of the Wedderburn target\n$(s, t, M_2, M_{31}, M_{211})$, in the row order of `coordM`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.coordMInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.coordMInv","kind":"def","line":1385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4WedderburnCoord.lean#L1385-L1389","doc":"The symbolic inverse $A^{-1}$ (sympy; **verified by Lean** via the\nentry-by-entry product identities of `HeckeH4WedderburnMul*.lean` —\nnothing is trusted from the computation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.H4.coordMInvRow23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.H4.coordMInvRow23","kind":"def","line":1357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeH4WedderburnCoord.lean#L1357-L1383","doc":"Row 23 of the symbolic inverse $A^{-1}$ (verified in\n`HeckeH4WedderburnMul*.lean`). ","signatureC